{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The platform's own record establishes arrival without any help from the exported trace. trip_record.platform_policy.arrival_marker is GPS_AUTO, and the events carry the platform's measured arrival — 'Driver GPS within 10m of pickup point. Speed 0 km/h. Auto-arrival confirmed.' at 08:43:00 — followed by rider_notified at 08:43:05 and wait_timer_started at 08:43:10. Under POL-NS-12 those PLATFORM_TELEMETRY events are a carrier independent of the exported gps_trace for POL-NS-01 limbs (b) and (c): arrival is established at 08:43:00 and the free waiting period is established as served when wait_timer_expired fired at 08:48:10.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-12", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.arrived_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trip_record terminates the trip at 08:51:00 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW and records no boarding: the interval from the 08:43:00 arrival to the 08:51:00 termination is 480 seconds, which is at or above both the free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec, 300 s) and the no-show threshold in force (platform_policy.no_show_threshold_sec, 480 s). POL-NS-01 limbs (c) and (d) are therefore carried, and the reason code is one of the three limb (d) recognises.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "payload.events.wait_timer_expired",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no false-arrival case to answer. The marker was auto-confirmed from the platform's own full-resolution measurement at 10 m from the pin and 0 km/h, not from a driver button press, and no fix in the exported trace can contradict it: the export is IMPAIRED (EV-GPS-00901, weight 0.6, issues LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD) and not one of its fixes reports a horizontal accuracy, so no fix in it is admissible to affirmatively place the driver more than 300 m from the pin or travelling at 15 km/h or more at the marker timestamp. POL-NS-05 is not engaged and no recomputation of the waiting clock is triggered.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00901", "EV-GPS-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "The export's zero qualifying-fix count cannot be read as the driver's absence. No fix in EV-GPS-00901 (IMPAIRED, weight 0.6, issues LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD) reports any horizontal accuracy, and POL-NS-02, read with the integrity block's accuracy_missing_treatment of UNKNOWN, makes an accuracy-less fix evidence of neither presence nor absence. derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count of 0 is the accuracy filter doing its work on this export, not a measurement that the driver was elsewhere at 08:43:00.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00901", "EV-TRIP-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02", "POL-NS-12"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no waiting-period shortfall, so POL-NS-06 has nothing to refund. derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.shortfall_sec of 300 s is computed from the same accuracy-less, impaired export (EV-GPS-00901, weight 0.6, issues LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD), whereas POL-NS-12 establishes the dwell as served from the platform's own wait_timer_started and wait_timer_expired events in trip_record. No accumulation under POL-NS-06(i) is needed for the driver's case, and the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00901-01 (MISSING, weight 0.0) is not relied on by this claim, directly or by assertion.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00901", "EV-GPS-00901", "EV-ADVIS-00901-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-12"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider because its limb (a) has nothing behind it. The chat log's six entries are five from the driver and one from the system, and not one locating or coordinating message was sent by the rider during the waiting window: no position, no entrance, no block or bay identifier, no request for the driver's position, no statement that the vehicle could not be seen.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even if a limb (a) message existed, limb (b) of POL-NS-04 fails. trip_record.in_app_calls records that the driver placed an in-app voice call to the rider at 08:47:05 (CALL-00901-001, rang 22 seconds, unanswered) before terminating the trip at 08:51:00, and the chat log carries the same call as MSG-00901-003. The driver both messaged and called; the rider answered neither.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00901", "EV-CHAT-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (c) of POL-NS-04 cannot be run at all on this record: the export carries no rider track (derived.rider_presence.available is false, with the reason that the source trace carries no rider track). On POL-NS-11 limb (c) is UNDECIDABLE — neither satisfied nor failed — so POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider on it; and notwithstanding POL-NS-08(b), the missing rider track is not the evidence for the driver's arrival or dwell and does not lower the confidence cap on a finding that rests on the driver's track. The rider was not shown to be elsewhere; the test simply could not be run.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-11", "POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.available",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "No wrong-entrance case is reached, so nothing in POL-NS-03 displaces the fee or the driver's payout. POL-NS-03 fires only where the stationary fixes lie outside the POL-NS-02 arrival radius but within 400 m, and the platform's own measurement places the driver 10 m from the pin at 0 km/h. In any event its limb (i) cannot be turned against the driver, because the chat log contains no rider statement of any entrance, block, tower or bay — the rider named no sub-location in the only communication channel that can carry one.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00901", "EV-CHAT-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's payout follows from the fee standing. POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, so under POL-NS-07 the driver is compensated at 80 percent of the fee in force for this trip — 0.8 x the 5.00 read from trip_record.platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd per fee_schedule.resolution_rule — which the fare ledger's own derived money block computes as driver_compensation 4.00 (EV-FARE-00901, IMPAIRED, weight 0.75, issue PARTIAL_RECORD). The anti-farming check cannot withhold it: the conjunctive test is read from driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d, which is null on this record, so the first limb ('4 or more') is not met and the check is undecidable here rather than tripped.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00901", "EV-DPROF-00901", "EV-TRIP-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.driver_compensation",
      "asserted_weight": 0.75
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no fare defect that could discount the fee. The fare_breakdown cancellation-fee line is 5.00 and coincides with the net amount the fee_schedule.resolution_rule produces for this trip from trip_record.platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged (EV-FARE-00901, IMPAIRED, weight 0.75, issue PARTIAL_RECORD; the reconciliation itself rests on EV-TRIP-00901 at weight 1.0).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00901", "EV-TRIP-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.75
    },
    {
      "text": "No POL-NS-09 escalation trigger is met, so this case is decidable and must not be sent to review. (b): no admissible artifact contradicts the arrival or the dwell — the export is unmeasurable, not contradictory; (c): rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d are both null, so the '2 or more' limb is not met; (d): rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is null and a null is not '3 or more', and the rider's lifetime prior_no_show_flags of 1 is not the field that limb reads; (e): the deciding facts for the fee rest on EV-TRIP-00901 at weight 1.0, which POL-NS-12 makes an independent carrier, so they are not carried solely by an artifact impaired under limbs (a) to (d) of POL-NS-08.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00901", "EV-RPROF-00901", "EV-DPROF-00901", "EV-GPS-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "Any attempt to build a finding on the rider's prior_no_show_flags of 1 is barred on the same footing as an uncited claim. POL-GEN-01 makes that field CONTEXT ONLY: it is a lifetime counter, it is a deliberate near-synonym trap for rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d, and it is that trailing-window field — which is null here — that POL-NS-09(d) names and that no one may substitute for.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The confidence cap does not approach the 0.70 floor. The deciding facts — arrival, dwell served and termination for a rider no-show — are carried by EV-TRIP-00901 and EV-CHAT-00901, both at weight 1.0, so on POL-GEN-02(2) the cap is 1.0. The only impaired artifacts on the driver's side of the ledger are the export (EV-GPS-00901, weight 0.6, issues LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD) and the fare ledger (EV-FARE-00901, weight 0.75, issue PARTIAL_RECORD), and both are disclosed in these claims, with their issue codes, rather than presented as clean.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00901", "EV-CHAT-00901", "EV-GPS-00901", "EV-FARE-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The outcome for this rider-filed dispute is NO_ACTION on the fee together with a driver payout. The ledger shows the 5.00 as CHARGED with refund_issued_sgd 0.00 (EV-FARE-00901, IMPAIRED, weight 0.75, issue PARTIAL_RECORD), so leaving the present state as it is leaves the charge in place and the rider's claim unsupported. Because the verified no-show also produces a driver payment, the emitted ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, and under POL-GEN-03 its amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd of 4.00 — it is not a refund to the filing party and is not netted against the fee.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00901", "EV-TRIP-00901"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 0.75
    }
  ]
}

