pends on computing the dwell from that same export. POL-NS-06 asks whether the effective dwell is shorter than the free waiting period; POL-NS-12 establishes that period as served from the platform's own wait_timer events, so there is no shortfall to refund. The rider's submission that POL-NS-12 reaches only POL-NS-01 limbs (b) and (c) and cannot touch POL-NS-06 is rejected for that reason. (3) The absent traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00901-01, MISSING, weight 0.0) only closes the accumulation route in POL-NS-06(i) and is not needed here. (4) The rider's own conduct: POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate her — limb (a) fails because the chat log (EV-CHAT-00901, weight 1.0) contains no locating or coordinating message from the rider (every entry is from the driver or the system), and limb (b) would fail in any event because the driver placed an in-app call at 08:47:05 (CALL-00901-001, rang 22 s, unanswered). POL-NS-11 makes limb (c) undecidable (no rider track) and neutral: the test could not be run, and I do not infer the rider was elsewhere. POL-NS-03 is not reached — the platform measured the driver 10 m from the pin, inside the STANDARD 50 m radius, so this is not a wrong-entrance case, and the rider named no sub-location in chat. POL-NS-05 is not engaged: the marker was GPS_AUTO at 10 m and 0 km/h and no fix in the impaired export can affirmatively place the driver outside the radius or in motion, so there is no false-arrival referral.\n\nThe money. Under POL-NS-07 the driver is compensated at 80 percent of the $5.00 fee in force for the trip (trip_record.platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd, read per fee_schedule.resolution_rule), which is $4.00; the fare ledger's own derived money block computes the same figure. The anti-farming check is not tripped: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is null, so the conjunctive test (4 or more AND a rate above 0.08) is not met, and compensation is not withheld. POL-GEN-01: rider_profile.prior_no_show_flags is a lifetime counter and context only — it is not the trailing-window field POL-NS-09(d) reads, and it is used for nothing in this ruling. No POL-NS-09 trigger is met: the deciding facts rest on EV-TRIP-00901 at weight 1.0 (POL-NS-12 makes it an independent carrier), so limb (e) is not engaged, and limbs (a), (b), (c) and (d) are not satisfied on these facts. The outcome for this rider-filed dispute is that the charge stands (EV-FARE-00901, weight 0.75, issue PARTIAL_RECORD, shows payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00), but because the driver is paid the emitted ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, with amount_sgd mirroring driver_compensation_sgd at $4.00 per POL-GEN-03 — it is not a refund to the filing party. The monetary effect of $4.00 is below the $8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically."
  },
