    "explanation": "To the rider (R-7823) and the driver (D-2398): this rider-filed dispute is over the $5.00 cancellation fee on trip TRIP-2026-09945. The fee stands and the driver is owed a platform payout of $4.00. Under POL-GEN-03 the emitted ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION and amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd at $4.00 — that figure is the money the ruling moves, not a refund to the rider, and the $5.00 charge stays in place (NO_ACTION on the fee).\n\nArrival and dwell (POL-NS-12, POL-NS-01). trip_record.platform_policy.arrival_marker is GPS_AUTO, and EV-TRIP-00901 (weight 1.0) carries the platform's own arrival event — 'Driver GPS within 10m of pickup point. Speed 0 km/h. Auto-arrival confirmed.' at 08:43:00 — followed by rider_notified 08:43:05, wait_timer_started 08:43:10, wait_timer_expired 08:48:10 and termination at 08:51:00. Under POL-NS-12 those PLATFORM_TELEMETRY events are the platform's own full-resolution measurement and a carrier independent of the exported trace for POL-NS-01 limbs (b) and (c). Arrival is therefore established at 08:43:00 and the 300-second free waiting period (platform_policy.free_wait_sec) is established as served; the termination at 08:51:00 is 480 seconds after arrival, meeting the 480-second platform_policy.no_show_threshold_sec. Limb (d) is met: no boarding, terminated by the driver under RIDER_NO_SHOW. POL-NS-01 holds in full.\n\nThe rider's POL-NS-02 argument is rejected. It is true that not one of the eight fixes in EV-GPS-00901 reports a horizontal accuracy, so derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count is 0; but an accuracy-less fix is evidence of neither presence nor absence, and POL-NS-12 exists precisely for a sparse, accuracy-less export where the platform itself confirmed arrival from its own stream. No admissible fix affirmatively places the driver outside the 50 m radius or moving at 15 km/h or more during the window, so POL-NS-05 is not engaged and there is no false-arrival referral. The rider's POL-NS-06 shortfall argument (300 s) is also rejected: POL-NS-06 fires only where the effective in-geofence dwell is shorter than the free waiting period, and the platform's wait timer establishes that period as served; the 0-second derived figure comes from the impaired export, not from a failed dwell.\n\nRider-exonerating routes (POL-NS-04, POL-NS-11, POL-NS-03). On POL-NS-04, the rider sent no locating or coordinating message in the waiting window, so limb (a) fails; independently, the driver placed an in-app call at 08:47:05 (CALL-00901-001, unanswered) before terminating, so limb (b) fails too. POL-NS-04 cannot exonerate the rider. POL-NS-11 is applied: no rider track was supplied, so limb (c) could not be run — it is undecidable and neutral, and it neither helps the rider nor impairs the driver's arrival and dwell evidence. POL-NS-03 is not reached, because the platform's measurement places the driver inside the arrival radius rather than at a wrong face of the venue.\n\nDriver payout (POL-NS-07). POL-NS-01 being satisfied and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displacing it, the driver is compensated at 80 percent of the fee in force: 0.8 x $5.00 = $4.00, matching the ferry ledger's own derived driver_compensation. The anti-farming check is not tripped — driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is null, so the first limb ('4 or more') is not met — and no other profile field may be used for that check.\n\nWeight and confidence (POL-GEN-02). The deciding facts — arrival, dwell served and termination for a rider no-show — are carried by EV-TRIP-00901 at weight 1.0, which POL-NS-12 makes independent of the export, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and my confidence is 0.9, above the 0.70 floor. Impaired artifacts: EV-GPS-00901 (weight 0.6, issues LOW_SAMPLE_RATE and PARTIAL_RECORD), EV-FARE-00901 (weight 0.75, issue PARTIAL_RECORD) and EV-ADVIS-00901-01 (MISSING, weight 0.0). None carries the deciding fact; the fare ledger's $5.00 line reconciles with the fee in force, so POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged, and the missing advisory is cited only for the absence itself.\n\nProfile fields (POL-GEN-01). The rider's prior_no_show_flags of 1 is context only and is not used as a ground; no citation of it affects this ruling.\n\nEscalation and execution. No POL-NS-09 trigger is met — confidence is above the floor, no admissible artifact contradicts the arrival or dwell, the counterparty-dispute fields are null, no_show_disputes_30d is null (and prior_no_show_flags is not that field), and the deciding facts rest on evidence at weight 1.0 rather than solely on an impaired artifact. No clause produces a referral. Under POL-GEN-05 the monetary effect of $4.00 does not exceed the $8.00 execution threshold, so this provisional ruling executes automatically, subject to the appeal route under POL-GEN-04."
  },
